## Context

Follow-up of 1392 (PR #2081). The author viewed the polished d77349fe page
("Much better!") and asked, 2026-10-31: distinguish tool calls by class, a
sticky first column with dynamic labels keyed to a red line, and bar labels
that stay on screen when scrolling a long agent bar.

In d77349fe, 884 of ~1100 tool calls are Bash, and a Bash event carries only
its description (`args.detail`), not the command. The command is available
where `scripts/trace_events.py` reads the tool_use block input (around line
240), so the class is computed there and travels as one additive field.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Each tool event carries a class, computed in `trace_events.py` from the
      tool name and (for shell calls) the command text:
      `subagent` (Skill, Agent), `worker` (shell launching a headless
      coder/reviewer: `codex exec`, `claude -p`, seat/gaze/gate launchers),
      `tests` (pytest, make check/lint/check-fast), `file` (Read/Edit/Write/
      Grep/Glob and Codex read/grep/apply_patch equivalents), `other`.
      Codex `exec` shell calls are classified like Bash by their command.
- [ ] The JSON export gains that field in `args` (additive only; every other
      byte of each event unchanged — test on a fixture); Perfetto still loads it
- [ ] The HTML colours tool bars by class, the legend lists each class, and the
      tooltip names it
- [ ] Unit tests for the classifier on representative commands, including a
      negative (a command that mentions pytest in a string but runs grep → not tests,
      or document the chosen precedence)
- [ ] Sticky label column: lane labels stay visible while scrolling horizontally
- [ ] A red vertical cursor at the middle of the viewport; each lane's label in
      the sticky column shows the agent (or call) under that cursor, updating on
      scroll, zoom and minimap moves
- [ ] A bar label for a long agent span sticks to the left edge of the visible
      area while the bar extends off-screen left
- [ ] Self-contained page still (no external URL); existing tests pass
- [ ] Rendered for d77349fe-10eb-46dd-a58c-d5723e771c4d, headless Firefox
      screenshot; the author checks interaction
- [ ] An agent bar's label appends the agent's model (e.g. "gaze seat correctness · gpt-6-luna") when
      the bar's on-screen width leaves room for it; it drops the model first, then truncates, as the bar
      narrows. Recomputed on zoom. The sticky label applies to the extended label too.
